No ascending non-priest character of mine has *ever* been level 30.
(Priests practically can't avoid being level 30...) 
I'm usually only level 18 or so at the castle.  And I'm not bragging.
I'm not a particularly good player.

BTW: My friends and I brag about our most challenging ascentions.  Our
     weakest games and characters that somehow made it.  We are unimpressed
     with people who leprichaun-ize priests, or nurse it up to ridiculous
     amounts, etc.  The challenge goes away.  It becomes boring.

I just want to point out to the newbies that your character doesn't have
to be that tough!  This has ALWAYS been a problem with this news-group.
People only talk about ascending with mondo-characters.

It's possible to ascend with a merely good character if you play smart!

To be honest, here is my formula for success:

1.  A blessed bag of holding
2.  Lots of holy water
3.  Blank scrolls and a blessed magic marker.
    (Blessed scroll of genocide for "L",  Blessed scrolls of enchant weapon.)
4.  Gray dragon scale mail.
5.  Speed boots.
6.  Either conflict or some form of taming.  ("Destroy the thief...")
7.  Some reflection.

Note that I'm not saying that my characters need all this before gehennom.
But they usually end up having most of this stuff by then, and before they 
ascend, they usually have all 7 of these things...  (For some reason,
I have a hard time getting reflection before fighting Archons.  My friend
gets a Shield of Reflection in almost every damn game before level 15!)

Everything else is icing.

>I absolutely have to have a PYEC and a WoP before I consider a game to be 
>winnable/enjoyable.

So, you're saying that it's not enjoyable if it's particularly challenging?

It's FUN to have to run away from the occaional Titan-minotaur-master_lich-
Archon combination.  A totally thrasher character can be BORING!

